          365125,
          10515600,
          1325563
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "How does it work?\nYou give it a bunch of words\nWhat are words to a computer? A bunch of random numbers \nJust make sure you don’t use the same numbers for each word.\nA bunch of number is called a vector. The vector could have 1024 numbers.\nSo if the words are “chickens cackle  and ducks ___”\nAnd the system, if it knows English will spit out a vector of 10000 numbers, each the probability that each word of English could be the next word.\n",
